From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:56:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vulkan): gate Q5_K mat-vec activation hoist to
 NUM_COLS<=3 (R48 phase 1b)

HQ paired the two arms on one binary over 3 quiet interleaved rounds: n=1..3
reads a wash to +5%, but n=4..8 loses 30% to 180% on every shape measured. That
is the NUM_COLS>=4 register spill the phase-1 report named as the risk - the
hoisted arm keeps NUM_ROWS x 26 floats live across the whole column loop.

Host-side gate only, no shader change: the f32_f32 and f16_f32 Q5_K dmmv
registrations now pass the hoist spec constant as 1 only for pipelines with
NUM_COLS <= 3, and 0 for wider ones. GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0 still forces every
width to 0, so the one-binary opt-out is unchanged. The device-init receipt line
now reads "ON (n<=3)".

test-backend-ops test -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p "type_a=q5_K": 61/61, 0 FAIL,
both arms (r48-evidence/61-*, 62-*).

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-234 R48 Q5_K phase 1b, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - hoist gated to NUM_COLS<=3 after HQ pairing showed n>=4 spill (-30..-180%); re-pair owed
Lane: lane-234
